{"id":"s3.2.1","slug":"converting-integers-bases","title":"Converting Integers","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">This section covers the two main processes for converting integers between bases.</p><p class=\"mb-4\"><strong>Base-n to Base-10:</strong> To convert a number from base-n to base-10, you expand it as a sum of powers of n. For example, $123_6 = 1 \\times 6^2 + 2 \\times 6^1 + 3 \\times 6^0 = 36 + 12 + 3 = 51_{10}$.</p><p class=\"mb-4\"><strong>Base-10 to Base-n:</strong> To convert from base-10 to base-n, you repeatedly divide the number by the highest possible power of n, recording the quotient as a digit and using the remainder for the next step with the next lower power of n. For example, to convert $51_{10}$ to base-6, the highest power of 6 that divides it is $6^2=36$. $51 \\div 36 = 1$ with a remainder of 15. The next digit is $15 \\div 6 = 2$ with a remainder of 3. The last digit is $3 \\div 1 = 3$. So, $51_{10} = 123_6$.</p>","summary":"This section covers the two main processes for converting integers between bases.","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem converting an integer from base-n to base-10 or vice-versa.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Convert $212_5$ to base 10.","answer":"57","kind":"exact","tags":["bases","conversions"]},{"id":2,"text":"Convert 108 to base 4.","answer":"1230","kind":"exact","tags":["bases","conversions"]},{"id":3,"text":"Convert $2004_5$ to base 10.","answer":"254","kind":"exact","tags":["bases","conversions"]},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate $3^4 + 3$ in base 9.","answer":"103","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","bases","conversions"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $2^4 + 2$ in base 4.","answer":"102","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","bases","conversions"]},{"id":6,"text":"Convert 82 to base 5.","answer":"312","kind":"exact","tags":["bases","conversions"]},{"id":7,"text":"Calculate $4^3 + 4$ in base 4.","answer":"1010","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","bases","conversions"]},{"id":8,"text":"Convert 24 to base 2.","answer"